{"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/segmentspecencoding\/segmentspecbatchencoder"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"abstract":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder","isActive":true},{"text":" of the Segment spec’s batch call, so an ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"can send events to Segment, RudderStack, Customer.io Data Pipelines, or another endpoint that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"takes Segment’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"POST \/v1\/batch"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"externalID":"s:19SegmentSpecEncoding0aB12BatchEncoderV","roleHeading":"Structure","title":"SegmentSpecBatchEncoder","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SegmentSpecBatchEncoder","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","modules":[{"name":"SegmentSpecEncoding"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SegmentSpecBatchEncoder"}],"remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Traffluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/SegmentSpecBatchEncoder.swift#L91","fileName":"SegmentSpecBatchEncoder.swift"},"symbolKind":"struct"},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/SegmentSpecBatchEncoder","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Initializers","title":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/SegmentSpecBatchEncoder\/init(plan:limit:)"],"generated":true},{"anchor":"Instance-Methods","title":"Instance Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/SegmentSpecBatchEncoder\/requests(for:)"],"generated":true},{"anchor":"Type-Aliases","title":"Type Aliases","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/SegmentSpecBatchEncoder\/Failure"],"generated":true},{"anchor":"Type-Properties","title":"Type Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/SegmentSpecBatchEncoder\/batchLimit","doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/SegmentSpecBatchEncoder\/transientStatuses"],"generated":true},{"anchor":"Type-Methods","title":"Type Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/SegmentSpecBatchEncoder\/outcome(of:for:)"],"generated":true}],"relationshipsSections":[{"type":"conformsTo","kind":"relationships","title":"Conforms To","identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder","doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/s16SendableMetatypeP"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SegmentSpecBatchEncoder","kind":"identifier"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"overview","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Make the destination with one of the factories, which fill in the endpoint, the credentials’"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"header field, this encoder and its limits:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/segment(writeKey:region:plan:backoff:clock:)","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/rudderStack(writeKey:dataPlane:plan:backoff:clock:)","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/customerIO(apiKey:region:plan:backoff:clock:)","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":":"}]},{"code":["let segment = try HTTPDestination.segment(","    writeKey: writeKey,","    region: .us,  \/\/ or .eu, where the workspace is","    plan: plan)"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The body is a JSON object of content type "},{"code":"application\/json","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" with one member, "},{"code":"batch","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", an array"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of track calls, one per record, oldest first, with these members:"}]},{"header":"row","type":"table","rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Member","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Holds"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"anonymousId","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The record’s session, its "},{"code":"SessionKey","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", as a lowercase UUID string; the record’s own "},{"code":"EventRecord\/id","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" when its context has no session"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"context","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The standard context, in the spec’s field names (below), and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ip"},{"text":" as ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\"0.0.0.0\""}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"event"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The event’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Event\/name"},{"type":"text","text":", as it is"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"messageId","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The record’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EventRecord\/id"},{"type":"text","text":", as a lowercase UUID string; a redelivered record keeps it"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"properties"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The event’s stored properties, by name","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"request_ip"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"\"0.0.0.0\"","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", in RudderStack’s calls alone","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"timestamp","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"When the event was tracked, in ISO 8601 with milliseconds, in UTC","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"type","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\"track\""}],"type":"paragraph"}]]]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The session is the only identifier sent: there is no "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"userId"},{"type":"text","text":", no "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"identify"},{"type":"text","text":" call, no traits,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and no "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"context.device.id"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"advertisingId"},{"type":"text","text":". An endpoint counts a user per "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"anonymousId"},{"type":"text","text":", so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"its anonymous users are sessions. A record with no session (one tracked by a tracker without"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Enricher.sessions()"},{"type":"text","text":") is its own anonymous user, linked to nothing: the spec rejects a call"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with neither a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"userId"},{"type":"text","text":" nor an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"anonymousId"},{"type":"text","text":". A record a store recovers after a relaunch keeps"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"its session, so it goes out with the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"anonymousId"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"messageId"},{"type":"text","text":" of its first send. Segment"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"deduplicates calls by "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"messageId"},{"type":"text","text":" over about the last 24 hours, and drops most duplicates"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"rather than all, so a recovered record Segment had already stored before the app ended is most"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"likely not stored again. RudderStack’s and Customer.io’s references don’t say whether they"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"deduplicate. The record’s vendor identifier"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and trace context, and any other context value, aren’t sent."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"context.ip"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\"0.0.0.0\""},{"text":" in every call, which the spec reads as the user’s address, so","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Segment records no address from the request. RudderStack fills in a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"request_ip"},{"text":" member from","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the request unless the call has one, even when ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"context.ip"},{"text":" is set, and passes it on to its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"destinations, so RudderStack’s calls also carry ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"request_ip"},{"text":" as ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\"0.0.0.0\""},{"text":". Customer.io’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"references don’t say whether ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"context.ip"},{"text":" takes the place of the address it reads from an HTTP","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"request. No call to Segment or Customer.io carries ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"request_ip"},{"text":", which their specs don’t have.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"No ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sentAt"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"originalTimestamp"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"channel"},{"text":" is sent. Without ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sentAt"},{"text":" the endpoint takes","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"timestamp"},{"text":" as it is, uncorrected for the device’s clock; it is left out on purpose, as a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"retried request sends the same body again, whose ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sentAt"},{"text":" would be the first attempt’s.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"RudderStack, whose references list all three as required, fills them in from when it received","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the call.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Properties are read through the event’s schema in ","type":"text"},{"code":"plan","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", as ","type":"text"},{"code":"PropertyReader","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" reads them. A","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/Sensitive","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" value is never sent, whatever the record reveals: the property is left","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"out, an element of an array is ","type":"text"},{"code":"null","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and one inside a type the plan can’t map is ","type":"text"},{"code":"null","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"context"},{"text":" holds these members, for each of the keys the record’s context has a value for:","type":"text"}]},{"header":"row","type":"table","rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Member","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Key"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Holds"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"app"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ApplicationKey"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"namespace"},{"type":"text","text":", the bundle identifier, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"version"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"build"},{"type":"text","text":", each left out when "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":"; no "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"app"},{"type":"text","text":" when all three are"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"device"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DeviceKey"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"model"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"type"},{"type":"text","text":", the platform as Segment’s Swift library names it: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ios"},{"type":"text","text":" for a phone or pad, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"macos"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tvos"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"watchos"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"visionos"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"locale"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"LocaleKey","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The locale’s BCP 47 identifier, such as "},{"code":"en-US","type":"codeVoice"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"network","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"NetworkKey","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"wifi","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"cellular","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", whether the connection is each","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"os","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"OperatingSystemKey","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"name","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"version","type":"codeVoice"}]}]]]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A record the encoder can’t write is left out of the request, and the batch’s other records are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sent: one whose event and version "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"plan"},{"type":"text","text":" doesn’t describe, one whose event name is one of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Customer.io’s semantic events, which delete or suppress people and devices, one whose event"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"isn’t "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Encodable"},{"type":"text","text":", one that holds a value JSON can’t, one whose timestamp has no ISO 8601 form,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and one too large for a call ("},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/SegmentSpecEncodingError"},{"type":"text","text":"). "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/SegmentSpecBatchEncoder\/requests(for:)"},{"type":"text","text":" returns them as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SkippedRecord"},{"type":"text","text":"s, which "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" logs and reports on its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"dropReports"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/SegmentSpecBatchEncoder\/requests(for:)"},{"type":"text","text":" splits a batch into requests within the encoder’s limit, "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/SegmentSpecBatchEncoder\/batchLimit"},{"type":"text","text":" by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"default, and makes none for a batch with no record it can write, so "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" sends"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"nothing for it. A record sent again keeps its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"messageId"},{"type":"text","text":". The bytes are the same for the same"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"records on every run and platform: no whitespace, object members in the order of their names’"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"UTF-8 bytes."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding"]]},"sections":[],"references":{"doc://HTTPDestinations/documentation/HTTPDestinations/BatchEncoder":{"url":"\/documentation\/httpdestinations\/batchencoder","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"BatchEncoder"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"BatchEncoder","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"BatchEncoder"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"What turns a batch of records in